SupraLINUX KAuth packaging
===========================

Authority:
- KDE upstream 6.30.0 selects KAuth source, behavior and dependencies.
- Ubuntu 26.04/Resolute is the platform/provider and Debian-package compatibility baseline.
- Debian packaging is a technical reference only.

Linux backend profile:
- KAUTH_BACKEND_NAME=POLKITQT6-1
- KAUTH_HELPER_BACKEND_NAME=DBUS
- Fake backend fallback is not accepted when the selected Polkit provider is available.

Retained Framework predecessors:
- Extra CMake Modules 6.30.0-0supralinux3
- KCoreAddons 6.30.0-0supralinux4
- KWindowSystem 6.30.0-0supralinux4

The build runner supplies the exact retained PASS .deb artifacts to sbuild.
Ubuntu must not silently replace those Framework predecessors.

Symbols:
The libKF6AuthCore.so.6 symbols file is imported at source-package assembly
from Debian kf6-kauth 6.30.0-1's debian.tar.xz, whose complete tarball SHA-256
is pinned in the campaign manifest. This avoids inventing a symbols baseline
while keeping Debian as a non-authoritative technical packaging reference.

The helper-install-dir patch preserves the Debian-family helper layout while
keeping upstream KAuth behavior intact.

Symbols portability adjustment
------------------------------

The second real build passed all 6 CTest entries and reached dh_makeshlibs.
Resolute's compiler/LTO combination does not emit two RTTI/vtable symbols for
KAuth::AuthBackend::Private that Debian's 6.30.0-1 symbols template records as
mandatory. The class is defined only in src/AuthBackend.cpp and is not public
header API.

SupraLINUX keeps Debian's complete 6.30 symbols template as the baseline, pins
its SHA-256, and changes only those two implementation-private symbols to
(optional=private). Existing optional=templinst entries remain untouched. No
public KAuth symbol is deleted, renamed, version-weakened or made optional.
